cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TDA Real-Time Monitoring: a pre-registered protocol for topological anomaly detection in financial markets"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Takagi
    given-names: Keishi
    email: keishi6903@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5733-333X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/keishi-takagi/tda-monitoring"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered real-time monitoring protocol for topological anomalies in
  financial markets, companion to the Takagi (2026) TDA paper series.
  Detection rules and computation parameters were fixed in the initial commit
  and are versioned separately from the implementation. The repository
  accumulates an out-of-sample record of rule-triggered detections, per-run
  metadata, and an append-only log of observations and of occasions on which
  the protocol's own discipline was tested.
keywords:
  - topological data analysis
  - persistent homology
  - pre-registration
  - financial markets
  - out-of-sample validation
license: MIT
